# JOURNEY · hand the keyboard to a botfish: a Reflex Arc and a Command Module bought at the bench and
# installed on one fish, the Arc's fire line wired to the module's fire in the panel, /console hands the
# keys over, a tapped SPACE makes the fish say glup glup, q is only a key, ESC gives the editor back.
# Budget: Computer $8,000 + botfish $7,700 + Reflex Arc $7,700 + Command Module $1,400 = $24,800 of
# $40,000. Each extra acting fish (botfish + module) is $9,100, so two fit ($33,900) and three do not.
# Panel fields: listens, drives, Command Module fire, eight Reflex Arc keys, its eight pins, trigger, 1..8.
# One botfish, so the install picker's ENTER picks it.

clear
include scenes/start-with-a-stake.play
include scenes/grow-a-matrixtank.play
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Reflex Arc" Peripherals
include scenes/buy-at-the-bench.play "Command Module" Hands
include scenes/take-a-fish.play botfish pad

run /consume reflex arc
expect Reflex Arc to the botfishes
key enter
absent to the botfishes
run /consume command module
key enter
absent to the botfishes

run /freeze "Pad"
run /nudge "Pad" 200 20
run /nudge "Pad" -15 0

run /program "Pad"
expect listens
key down 2
expect Command Module
type glup
key down 13
expect right[1]
type glup
key down 5
type /say "glup glup"
snap the Arc's fire line and the module's fire share one channel, and the script speaks
key enter
absent listens

run /console "Pad"
expect console Pad
expect SPACE fire
expect ESC leave
snap the console bar replaces the editor and names every key it listens for
type q
expect console Pad
key space
release space
tick 40
expect glup glup
snap a tapped SPACE fired the module and Pad says glup glup
key esc
absent console Pad
absent ESC leave
